Yes, we've got superpowers.

41
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:19,630
Superpowers.

42
00:02:19,713 --> 00:02:22,260
Yes, we're the superpowers.

43
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:24,510
Superpowers.

44
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:27,740
Yes, we're the superpowers.

45
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:38,261
It's no wonder you're frustrated.

46
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:41,700
Every time you try to take
a stand, I knock you down.

47
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:45,657
Did you notice when you
tried to throw a left punch?

48
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:47,097
I targeted your left shoulder.

49
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:49,117
And when you tried to throw a right punch.

50
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:55,577
I targeted your right shoulder, all
of your efforts have been in vain;

51
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:59,177
you are nothing but a fool
drowning in your own failure.

52
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:03,240
This is what it's like when your
enemy can predict your every move.

53
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:07,828
Forcing you to lash out in
desperation is just the appetizer.

54
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:11,437
Whether you throw a left
kick or a right kick,

55
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:14,520
I will strike you before
you can even make contact.

56
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:20,300
And I won't let up until I
see your heart burst in two.

57
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:30,040
There's intent behind every attack.

58
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:36,960
A hint, too.

59
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:44,460
Don't attack your foe blindly.

60
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:46,150
Focus.

61
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:52,280
Die!

62
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:13,680
It's as I suspected.

63
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:25,900
It's infrequent, but he's able
to see the future, same as me.

64
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:39,580
Son of a biscuit!

65
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:41,210
What's wrong?

66
00:04:41,293 --> 00:04:42,620
I screwed up big time!

67
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:44,017
It totally slipped my mind,

68
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:47,557
but I was supposed to pipe roses of
whipped cream on the top of the cake!

69
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:48,993
Let me take care of it.

70
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:52,020
Pastry bag, please? Yes, sir!

71
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:54,110
Skywalk!

72
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:10,700
So cool! It's wonderful!

73
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:14,520
Bam! It's ready.

74
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:17,920
Wow! Nice work!

75
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:19,380
It's finally complete.

76
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:21,717
The ultimate wedding cake masterpiece.

77
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,440
So how's it look? Yeah!

78
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,200
Incredible, Lili!

79
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,206
Smells so good I could paint!

80
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:31,480
Agreed, dammit!

81
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:32,720
It came out great!

82
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:36,157
This cake don't even need to
be full of poison after all.

83
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:40,220
That big broad's gonna drop
after one bite. Arrivederci!

84
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,080
The cake's all done.

85
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:50,580
Made it just in time. You okay?

86
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:56,840
What happened?

87
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:58,037
You feeling all right?

88
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:00,296
Why are they all collapsing suddenly?

89
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:03,467
They really must have
worked their asses off.

90
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:19,840
Don't bother getting up.

91
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:22,158
We already know all about your plan.

92
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:26,500
Kaku Island, 1am, right?

93
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:28,896
Not that it matters.

94
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:32,671
Your friends won't even get
the chance to reach the island.

95
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:38,121
Soon they'll be met by my brother's fleets
waiting in anticipation of their arrival.

96
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:42,912
And the same fate is in store for you,
should you manage to escape somehow.

97
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:46,000
Doesn't matter.

98
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:47,590
Hmm?

99
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,860
I'm still gonna make it out
of here, one way or another.

100
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:00,701
You sound confident, like
it's destined to happen.

101
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:08,360
By the way, Pudding and Chiffon, couldn't
have done it without you. Thanks a ton.

102
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:15,191
Seriously, with this cake, I'll
definitely save my friends.

103
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,637
There's no way you know that for sure!

104
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:23,997
Yeah, the cake is finished
and all, but big whoop!

105
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:27,021
I hate to tell ya, but
they might be dead already!

106
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:29,777
Besides, he even knows if Mama
will like the cake or not.

107
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:30,690
Honestly,

108
00:07:30,773 --> 00:07:32,297
this seems like a big
waste of time bringing

109
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:35,440
this Serious excuse of
a cake to your Sanji.

110
00:07:38,020 --> 00:07:40,138
Tell him you didn't mean it pudding.

111
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:41,750
Oh.

112
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:49,260
Whatever the case is it's
too late to worry now!

113
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:01,780
You can't run away!

114
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:09,540
I want my wedding cape! Now! Let's rumble!

115
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,133
Time for monster point!

116
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:18,100
I'll make sure she doesn't come back.

117
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:20,540
What the hell? A monster?

118
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:22,120
They have monsters?

119
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:23,300
Since when?

120
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:26,820
Napoleon, are you prepared? Extend!

121
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:32,180
Hey, Chopper!

122
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:34,040
Everyone, listen up!

123
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:36,262
Buy us as much time as possible!

124
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:37,430
Sure.

125
00:08:37,513 --> 00:08:38,518
Sounds like a plan.

126
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:40,720
We're always right here beside you.

127
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:47,840
Until that moment arrives, we will
endure whatever she can heave our way.

128
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:50,557
Big Mom doesn't know it's coming her way.

129
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:52,760
The greatest cake ever made.

130
00:08:53,140 --> 00:08:55,420
I swear I will beat you.

131
00:08:57,020 --> 00:08:59,520
Then I'll go and rejoin my crew.

132
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:06,500
Because my friends believe in me.

133
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:12,720
I'll slice you in two!

134
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:16,930
No!

135
00:09:24,860 --> 00:09:26,566
It's time to use Ghost Sword!

136
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:36,200
Oh, please!

137
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:40,720
Oh, please!

138
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:42,900
I'm not here!

139
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:46,380
Get out!

140
00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:59,137
Chopper! Stop! You're hurt!

141
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:00,800
Don't worry, I'm okay.

142
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,960
Big Mom, do your worst.

143
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:07,740
I can at least drag you into the
murky waters with me before I go down.

144
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:11,944
You're a fiery one, aren't you?

145
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:16,475
Let's see if this is still a good on
that threat after you witness this.

146
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:40,560
Oh, no.

147
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:41,860
But how?

148
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:49,800
At that size, no amount
of seawater will help.

149
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:52,600
They're so, so fiercely. Unreal.

150
00:10:58,060 --> 00:11:00,417
Let's see how far you guys can run now.

151
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:04,400
We can't stick around, or we'll
burn up alongside the summit.

152
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:08,057
It's a shame, since we've
managed to make it this far.

153
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:10,777
Not to mention, Sanji
will be here any minute.

154
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:13,217
It's been fun, you guys.

155
00:11:13,300 --> 00:11:14,220
Really?

156
00:11:15,860 --> 00:11:17,840
Now, where's my cake?

157
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:35,380
Wow, where is that coming from?

158
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:39,500
Stop getting up.

159
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:41,240
How do you expect to win?

160
00:11:45,140 --> 00:11:49,199
His observation Haki is nearly
sharp enough to compete with my own.

161
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:13,720
If I don't put an end to him soon,
the unthinkable could happen.

162
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:38,360
It's them!

163
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:42,840
They're here!

164
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:46,540
It's their ship!

165
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:49,520
You see that?

166
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:50,560
It's the cake!

167
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:57,437
Sancti's crew really pulled through!

168
00:12:57,520 --> 00:12:58,461
They brought it!

169
00:12:58,580 --> 00:13:01,280
The lights, Sancti! Sancti!

170
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:03,670
Mama?

171
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:05,380
Is that...

172
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:09,180
Goodness, that smells good!

173
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:16,460
Hey, Blackleg, looks like
we got eyes on your ship.

174
00:13:16,980 --> 00:13:20,240
Stinking Prometheus, look
how freaking huge you got.

175
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:21,897
Powered up by Big Mom's soul.

176
00:13:21,980 --> 00:13:24,804
Hate to say it, but look
who he's toting around.

177
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,412
That's Big Mom up there.

178
00:13:26,920 --> 00:13:28,660
Father, there's a fleet, too.

179
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,920
I can spot Patty Sparrow and Bob O 'Wall.

180
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:35,700
Plus Smoothie and her crew, too. I see.

181
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:38,821
No matter how you look at
it, that spells trouble.

182
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:42,536
Seems like the Straw Hat
ships in rough shape, though.

183
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:47,660
All right. Ready, boys? Yeah!

184
00:13:48,380 --> 00:13:50,277
Remember, this is Big Mom.

185
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:53,400
You can't fool around with her. Capisce?

186
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:56,180
You plug that dame full of lead.

187
00:13:56,420 --> 00:13:57,580
Then light her up.

188
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:00,670
Gee.

189
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:09,980
Oh, Mommy!

190
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:12,300
I've come to save you!

191
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:14,130
Tang.

192
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:16,117
Look, Blacklick.

193
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:19,553
Seems like your crew's been
running from Big Mom all day.

194
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:21,525
Wow, you really hung in there.

195
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:23,820
Your captain ain't even with them.

196
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:25,190
Mom!

197
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:28,065
There's a Noodle Man on board.

198
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:30,122
He's releasing some weird power.

199
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:31,880
I doubt that's Haki.

200
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:35,301
But why are they arriving
on Benji's ship, though?

201
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:38,540
I think someone's dancing on the bow.

202
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:40,280
Who cares about that?

203
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:42,400
What really matters is the cake.

204
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:44,440
I'll be damned.

205
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:46,977
They managed to recreate the wedding cake

206
00:14:47,060 --> 00:14:50,780
down to every last
lickety-dollop and detail.

207
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:54,600
Hope it passes the taste test.

208
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:57,196
Nothing else can stop Mama's madness.

209
00:14:57,580 --> 00:14:58,410
Although,

210
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:00,624
Buggy is standing right there.

211
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:02,780
That cake is bound to be poisoned.

212
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:07,860
What should I do?

213
00:15:10,940 --> 00:15:15,380
Thanks to the smell she backed
off, I really got lucky.

214
00:15:16,980 --> 00:15:19,440
Man, I thought I was a gunner for sure.

215
00:15:21,620 --> 00:15:24,697
Should we attempt to destroy
the replacement wedding cake?

216
00:15:24,780 --> 00:15:25,957
No, if we do that,

217
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:27,777
then there will be no stopping Mama from

218
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:30,600
lickety-liquidating
Toto Land as we know it.

219
00:15:32,060 --> 00:15:33,780
But if the cake is poisoned,

220
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:37,597
then both the country and the pirate
operation will crumble without her.

221
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:38,740
What should I do?

222
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:41,400
This is a lickety-lose-lose situation.

223
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:47,557
Hey Black Leg, you got yourself a deal,

224
00:15:47,640 --> 00:15:50,577
Paulie, and don't worry—we'll
step aside, promise.

225
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:51,490
We

226
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:55,117
can handle the cake from here and there;

227
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:57,657
won't be any aggression
till that bird has a fill.

228
00:15:57,740 --> 00:15:58,570
But

229
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:06,217
I'm free to do as I please afterwards,
yeah, that's correct—I only had one job:

230
00:16:06,300 --> 00:16:09,177
the wedding cake—bake a new
one to calm big mom down.

231
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:13,037
Okay, let's do it all
right—we're ready, Sanji.

232
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:14,708
Coming then—hurry, the hell

233
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:19,377
up, unless you want to die!

234
00:16:19,460 --> 00:16:20,290
Hey pudding—take it easy.

235
00:16:20,373 --> 00:16:22,440
die hey pudding

236
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:26,140
take it easy

237
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,520
Thanks. You good?

238
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:33,540
For sure.

239
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:35,220
See you soon.

240
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:36,830
Chip on.

241
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:41,110
Robin!

242
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:42,848
We'd better make this fast!

243
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:46,120
Listen closely!

244
00:16:46,420 --> 00:16:49,077
Go quickly enough that
neither of my brothers notice!

245
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:49,990
Roger!

246
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:58,440
Would that be my wedding cake?

247
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:01,420
It's there!

248
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:06,840
I knew it had to be around! Quickly!

249
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:08,190
Yeah!

250
00:17:08,660 --> 00:17:09,490
Mama!

251
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:13,480
I can't see my cake!

252
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:15,920
Here she comes!

253
00:17:16,220 --> 00:17:18,120
Turn Starboy! Yes, sir!

254
00:17:19,140 --> 00:17:20,760
Go southwest at full speed!

255
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:22,620
Head toward Lock Island!

256
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:28,097
What the hell?!

257
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:29,400
Hey, Press, look!

258
00:17:29,700 --> 00:17:32,700
The ship with the cake has
suddenly changed course!

259
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:33,950
Why?!

260
00:17:34,033 --> 00:17:37,739
I think they're enticing Mama to
follow Bezzy's ship for some reason!

261
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:39,318
That's interesting.

262
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:41,980
Lickety-leading Mama away, are they?

263
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:46,197
Could it be that they are trying to
divide us by forcing us to split up?

264
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:47,110
Clever.

265
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:48,830
Yo-ho!

266
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:51,600
Hey there, you miss me?

267
00:17:52,300 --> 00:17:53,797
Sanji! It's Sanji!

268
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:55,940
I'm putting too! Sanji!

269
00:17:56,120 --> 00:17:58,357
We were barely hanging on by a thread.

270
00:17:58,440 --> 00:18:00,028
I thought we were done for.

271
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:02,200
I'm so glad you're safe.

272
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:08,000
Mama Bloom!

273
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:11,980
I love you too, Nami, my sweet honey pie.

274
00:18:12,580 --> 00:18:16,540
By the way, Sanji, why
were you on Veggie's ship?

275
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:20,400
Oh, yeah, long story.

276
00:18:20,780 --> 00:18:22,898
Where precisely is this ship headed?

277
00:18:24,260 --> 00:18:28,557
Nobody exactly knows what Big Mom will
do after she finishes eating the cake.

278
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:33,660
So Buggy and his men are luring her to
the closest island just to be safe. Huh?

279
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:36,528
Why would he willingly
volunteer to be bait?

280
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:38,936
What could he be getting out of this?

281
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:41,946
Well, he hasn't given
up on murdering her yet.

282
00:18:42,800 --> 00:18:43,630
Typical.

283
00:18:43,713 --> 00:18:44,543
Sounds like him.

284
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:48,117
Sonny's safety is the only
thing that matters to me.

285
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:51,906
If he can keep Big Mom away from
it, then I can't ask for more.

286
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:53,070
Do you get me?

287
00:18:54,940 --> 00:18:56,720
Just look, poor Sonny.

288
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:59,460
I'm sorry that I failed to protect it.

289
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:00,920
You can't say that!

290
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:03,517
We would have been lost
without you, Jinbei!

291
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,430
Take it back!

292
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:05,860
We can catch up later.

293
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:08,200
I'm just relieved you're all safe.

294
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:12,660
Anyway, what are Pedro and
Karen up to at the moment?

295
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:18,230
Well?

296
00:19:18,540 --> 00:19:20,980
Oh, uh, they're in the cabin.

297
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:24,918
Uh, and they're both wiped
out from all the fighting.

298
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:28,140
Press, what should we do?

299
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:29,300
What do we chase?

300
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:30,620
Brahat or Mama?

301
00:19:30,820 --> 00:19:33,397
We can't let him lickety
leave with his life.

302
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:34,657
Bada-bada-bada-bada-bada.

303
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:40,820
Hey, Press, it's me, Veggie.

304
00:19:41,380 --> 00:19:42,960
Veggie, you backstabber!

305
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:44,197
What are you up to?

306
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:47,960
Why the hell are you the one
lickety-lugging that cake around?

307
00:19:49,180 --> 00:19:50,768
Don't you worry about that.

308
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:53,137
I'll be dealing with Mama's hunger pains.

309
00:19:53,220 --> 00:19:58,680
I'll let her have her fill the cake until
she calms down. You rat! Liar! Traitor!

310
00:19:58,940 --> 00:20:00,157
What did you put in the cake?

311
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:01,797
You messed with it, didn't you?

312
00:20:01,880 --> 00:20:04,409
I assure you there's
nothing wrong with it.

313
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:07,265
Besides, Puddin had a
hand in making the thing.

314
00:20:07,380 --> 00:20:10,617
If that's the case, then tell
me where she is right now!

315
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:13,057
I wouldn't worry about
the details if I was you.

316
00:20:13,140 --> 00:20:16,097
Maybe you should focus on
taking care of Straw Hat.

317
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:18,580
I got things down pat on my head, eh?

318
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:20,117
What are you, son of a...

319
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,030
Calvick!

320
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:23,620
Fiji! Hello!

321
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:27,480
We're going after that
bastard, Bavawa! Huh?

322
00:20:27,940 --> 00:20:32,058
I'm 100 % positive he's plotting to
go through with the assassination!

323
00:20:32,660 --> 00:20:36,131
It's lickety-likely he's done
something to pudding as well.

324
00:20:36,220 --> 00:20:37,573
Do you think so, Pedos?

325
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:40,017
Maybe we should follow Straw Hat's ship.

326
00:20:40,100 --> 00:20:42,117
It will sink a cacao island anyway.

327
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:43,620
And besides,

328
00:20:44,020 --> 00:20:47,557
did you forget that we
have a certain someone

329
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:49,957
who we can count on to finish the mission?

330
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:51,520
Huh? Oh, yeah.

331
00:20:51,700 --> 00:20:52,994
Why won't you pick up?

332
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:54,517
Hey, Smoothie,

333
00:20:54,600 --> 00:20:59,012
I need to know if you're still a part
of the fleet trailing the Straw Hats.

334
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:02,000
Yeah, right on your tail, Pedos.

335
00:21:04,460 --> 00:21:08,872
I need you to stick to the Straw Hats
like your lickety-life depends on it.

336
00:21:11,460 --> 00:21:14,120
Boboar and I are going
after Buggy and Mama.

337
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:22,417
Squeeze every last drop of lickety life
from those rotten little trespassers.

338
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:26,157
Don't stop tormenting them until
they jump off the edge of sanity!

339
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:28,100
Do I make myself clear?

340
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:29,397
Abundantly so.

341
00:21:29,480 --> 00:21:34,421
Perlick: If that's what he wanted, then he
should have just asked me from the start.

342
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:36,497
Our poor brother, Press.

343
00:21:36,580 --> 00:21:38,360
Getting distracted, isn't he?

344
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:44,740
We should have stayed put on Cacao Island.

345
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:47,784
I was really enjoying all
the tea and chocolate.

346
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:49,720
He's just being impatient.

347
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:51,780
These men are such idiots.

348
00:22:00,540 --> 00:22:02,120
No time for complaining.

349
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:10,758
All right, let's prepare for battle.

350
00:22:11,040 --> 00:22:13,216
We're going to sink Straw Hat's ship.

351
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,920
We shall stop them before
they reach Kaku Island. Yeah!

352
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:19,390
Hmm.

353
00:22:19,940 --> 00:22:20,770
Mm-hmm.

354
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:25,900
They know it all?

355
00:22:26,100 --> 00:22:27,924
Even where we're meeting Luffy?

356
00:22:28,040 --> 00:22:31,380
Yeah, I bet Kaku Island's
surrounded with ships by now.

357
00:22:32,700 --> 00:22:33,530
Damn.

358
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:38,845
It appears that they are treating us as
a true threat, which is unusual for them.

359
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:42,765
This will be our final obstacle,
but likely our biggest as well.

360
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:47,779
We're gonna rescue Luffy no matter
what and then make a break for it.

361
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:48,870
However,

362
00:22:48,953 --> 00:22:53,488
we'll have to avoid their fleets at all
costs or else we're gonna be done for.

363
00:23:04,520 --> 00:23:06,140
You look pathetic.

364
00:23:24,500 --> 00:23:28,520
Your foot slipped, you amateur.

365
00:23:36,540 --> 00:23:37,660
Straw Hat!

366
00:23:39,060 --> 00:23:41,700
Oh, my plan is working!

367
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:56,780
Big bra!

368
00:24:09,120 --> 00:24:11,680
Did you know that I was helping all along?

369
00:24:11,860 --> 00:24:14,120
I hadn't realized that. Thank you.

370
00:24:14,460 --> 00:24:16,360
What a good girl you are.

371
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:23,120
Flampe, you truly are my favorite sister.

372
00:24:26,160 --> 00:24:29,080
Oh, man, I miss Clippers. I am cute.

373
00:24:36,800 --> 00:24:39,160
Just one moment of recklessness.

374
00:24:41,500 --> 00:24:43,540
That's what can decide a battle.

375
00:24:52,700 --> 00:24:54,860
Never let your guard down.

376
00:25:13,600 --> 00:25:15,320
Don't see another one!

377
00:25:24,180 --> 00:25:26,440
What's the matter, Straw Hat?

378
00:25:53,140 --> 00:25:56,199
Just when I was starting
to admit you were worth it.

379
00:25:57,260 --> 00:25:59,560
What a disappointment!

380
00:26:27,300 --> 00:26:29,060
Did I imagine that?

381
00:26:30,140 --> 00:26:32,000
I swear I saw it!

382
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:35,600
Imagination is part of it.

383
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:40,000
Beyond such tricks of the mind,
you will find observation, Haki.

384
00:26:46,520 --> 00:26:50,240
Basically, it's something you
learn to feel out subconsciously.

385
00:26:51,700 --> 00:26:52,582
Subconsciously?

386
00:27:00,380 --> 00:27:01,317
He's stood up?

387
00:27:01,400 --> 00:27:03,400
He's looking pretty shaky, though.

388
00:27:04,500 --> 00:27:06,120
Fine, one more I'll do it.

389
00:27:09,160 --> 00:27:13,984
This time I'll nail you with a numbing
needle ten times more potent than the last.

390
00:27:17,780 --> 00:27:20,662
This will show you for
wasting my brother's time.

391
00:27:20,760 --> 00:27:22,642
Drop dead, you dirty little ape.

392
00:27:29,100 --> 00:27:30,300
Numbin' Needle!

393
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:47,470
What?!

394
00:27:47,553 --> 00:27:49,220
My Needle was totally silent!

395
00:27:49,500 --> 00:27:51,440
How in the heck did he dodge?!

396
00:27:56,620 --> 00:27:59,160
The moron fell down anyway!

397
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:35,420
Keep it down.

398
00:28:35,640 --> 00:28:37,052
They're gonna notice us.

399
00:28:37,240 --> 00:28:38,740
But I can't help it.

400
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:40,060
Just look at him.

401
00:28:40,440 --> 00:28:42,040
Tramble like a newborn mom.

402
00:28:42,380 --> 00:28:44,020
It's such a pathetic sight.

403
00:28:44,920 --> 00:28:46,020
Wabble wabble.

404
00:28:48,060 --> 00:28:49,040
Knock it off.

405
00:28:49,380 --> 00:28:50,674
The kid's so laughing.

406
00:28:50,820 --> 00:28:52,077
Hey, look, look, look.

407
00:28:52,160 --> 00:28:53,417
He can't figure it out.

408
00:28:53,500 --> 00:28:57,597
He's drenched in blood and stumbling
around, but he doesn't know what hit him.

409
00:28:57,680 --> 00:28:58,700
That moron.

410
00:29:04,120 --> 00:29:07,260
His determination is
almost too much to stomach.

411
00:29:07,720 --> 00:29:09,308
Throw in the towel already.

412
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:14,030
Slumpay.

413
00:29:26,500 --> 00:29:27,330
Dammit.

414
00:29:39,440 --> 00:29:40,270
Whee!

415
00:29:40,353 --> 00:29:43,045
I think Big Brown might
be looking right at me!

416
00:29:43,220 --> 00:29:45,800
He's so cool, I just want to screw you!

417
00:29:51,580 --> 00:29:54,517
Don't get freaked out, but I
think he's coming this way.

418
00:29:54,600 --> 00:29:55,430
Really?

419
00:29:58,520 --> 00:29:59,640
Well done.

420
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:02,687
You're such a splendid
little sister, Flampe.

421
00:30:03,080 --> 00:30:04,000
Good girl.

422
00:30:04,760 --> 00:30:06,520
He's going to freeze me.

423
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:09,900
The day has finally come.

424
00:30:10,120 --> 00:30:11,560
I am so not ready.

425
00:30:12,960 --> 00:30:14,317
I see now.

426
00:30:14,400 --> 00:30:16,840
So it was you, Flampe.

427
00:30:20,900 --> 00:30:25,600
By using that blowgun you love so
much, you took away his mobility.

428
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:34,480
During our heated standoff, your
interference caused his focus to falter.

429
00:30:35,620 --> 00:30:38,260
I knew something felt off.

430
00:30:47,520 --> 00:30:51,696
That was when I landed the blow that
ripped a bloody hole in his torso.

431
00:30:56,140 --> 00:31:01,220
Do you really think that I'd want to
claim victory in such a dishonorable way?

432
00:31:01,480 --> 00:31:03,657
Are you seeing this crap, Lady Flumpe?

433
00:31:03,740 --> 00:31:05,916
The wounded animal's getting back up.

434
00:31:07,540 --> 00:31:09,040
Hey, that made me laugh.

435
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:10,230
It's trembling.

436
00:31:10,313 --> 00:31:12,520
Little baby deer walking for his body.

437
00:31:14,760 --> 00:31:19,172
Yeah, I can't wait to see General
Katakuri beat the crap out of this idiot!

438
00:31:21,500 --> 00:31:22,330
Obviously!

439
00:31:22,413 --> 00:31:24,257
It'll be another flawless victory!

440
00:31:24,340 --> 00:31:26,140
Kick his butt, big bro!

441
00:31:27,020 --> 00:31:27,850
Flop.

442
00:31:30,220 --> 00:31:32,120
It was you, wasn't it?

443
00:31:32,900 --> 00:31:33,760
That's right!

444
00:31:33,940 --> 00:31:34,770
It was me!

445
00:31:34,853 --> 00:31:36,700
I did it all for you!

446
00:31:37,860 --> 00:31:39,340
Aren't I just the cutest,

447
00:31:39,620 --> 00:31:43,417
sweetest, and most considerate
out of all of your little sisters?

448
00:31:43,500 --> 00:31:49,180
No one in the world is more perfect than
you and I get to be your save! Lucky me!

449
00:31:49,760 --> 00:31:52,320
I'll collect those haircuts now, please!

450
00:31:53,320 --> 00:31:54,220
Big bro!

451
00:31:58,280 --> 00:31:59,337
You idiots!

452
00:31:59,420 --> 00:32:00,760
What's so funny?

453
00:32:29,460 --> 00:32:31,860
What did you do that for?

454
00:32:33,300 --> 00:32:34,700
What the hell?

455
00:32:42,100 --> 00:32:44,280
I shouldn't have to tell you this.

456
00:32:47,820 --> 00:32:51,240
When a man goes to battle,
don't patronize him!

457
00:32:55,560 --> 00:32:57,148
Are you worried about that?

458
00:32:57,560 --> 00:32:58,390
Ow!

459
00:32:58,820 --> 00:33:00,920
I love you, gold man!

460
00:33:07,620 --> 00:33:12,680
If you laugh at a man fighting for his
life, then why not have a laugh at me, too?

461
00:33:22,620 --> 00:33:23,580
You suck!

462
00:33:37,560 --> 00:33:38,390
Agreed!

463
00:33:38,473 --> 00:33:39,480
What a bummer!

464
00:33:40,580 --> 00:33:41,410
Ew!

465
00:33:41,493 --> 00:33:42,323
That's your blood!

466
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:44,280
Why are you so gross?

467
00:33:45,060 --> 00:33:49,589
Where'd you put the calm, cool, and
collected big bro that I love and admire?

468
00:33:49,700 --> 00:33:51,994
What the hell has gotten into you, huh?

469
00:33:53,080 --> 00:33:55,020
Why would you stab yourself?

470
00:33:55,480 --> 00:33:57,040
You big lame ass!

471
00:33:57,180 --> 00:34:00,356
You are totally not the same
cut of curry that I know!

472
00:34:00,520 --> 00:34:01,720
Totally pathetic!

473
00:34:03,400 --> 00:34:05,760
You pelican eel looking bastard!

474
00:34:06,420 --> 00:34:08,620
That is what he looks like!

475
00:34:08,960 --> 00:34:11,897
Stop it, Lady Pompey! I'm gonna...

476
00:34:11,980 --> 00:34:13,880
I'm gonna pee my pants!

477
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:15,000
So gross!

478
00:34:15,340 --> 00:34:16,693
You really let me down!

479
00:34:19,420 --> 00:34:23,180
Here comes a pelican eel! Stay away!

480
00:34:23,560 --> 00:34:24,980
That kid's a monster!

481
00:34:25,380 --> 00:34:26,674
Don't let him get you!

482
00:34:34,540 --> 00:34:37,160
Hey, aren't you gonna say something?

483
00:34:57,860 --> 00:34:59,677
Hurry up and take some pictures!

484
00:34:59,760 --> 00:35:01,077
We gotta get the word out.

485
00:35:01,160 --> 00:35:03,689
Everyone needs to see
this messed up space!

486
00:35:11,300 --> 00:35:12,180
Come on!

487
00:35:12,320 --> 00:35:13,280
What's the rush?

488
00:35:13,500 --> 00:35:16,029
Well, you might hold
it still for a second.

489
00:35:17,780 --> 00:35:20,377
General Katakuri, can you
look over here real quick?

490
00:35:20,460 --> 00:35:23,166
That chum for me does
look like a pelican eel!

491
00:35:24,060 --> 00:35:28,740
The flawless big brother I once had
is dead to me now. You hear that?

492
00:35:29,300 --> 00:35:31,000
Die, Charlotte Katakuri!

493
00:35:31,360 --> 00:35:33,957
I'll send these photos
of your freaky face to

494
00:35:34,040 --> 00:35:37,460
every fan club never in
every island in Totoland!

495
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:40,457
How dare you splutter
your grimy blood on me!

496
00:35:40,540 --> 00:35:44,077
That's the price you pay for
snubbing your favorite little sister!

497
00:35:44,160 --> 00:35:46,537
I can't believe I
thought you were perfect!

498
00:35:46,620 --> 00:35:47,855
You're so disgusting!

499
00:35:48,140 --> 00:35:50,787
I'm ashamed to admit
that I'm related to you!

500
00:35:51,860 --> 00:35:53,440
You're both gonna get it,

501
00:35:53,540 --> 00:35:57,364
and don't think I forgot how you
ruined the tea party, Straw Hat!

502
00:35:58,220 --> 00:36:01,120
Just looking at your dumb
faces is annoying me!

503
00:36:01,420 --> 00:36:03,837
I'm aiming straight for
the heart this time!

504
00:36:03,920 --> 00:36:05,920
I hope you enjoy venomous needles!

505
00:36:06,120 --> 00:36:07,437
What have happened?!

506
00:36:07,520 --> 00:36:09,580
I'll never forgive you!

507
00:36:09,700 --> 00:36:11,818
I won't let you walk away from this!

508
00:36:16,240 --> 00:36:18,840
I've had enough of everyone's commentary.

509
00:36:20,820 --> 00:36:23,660
They won't be able to
stand after this anyway.

510
00:36:47,180 --> 00:36:51,600
Conqueror's monkey, pet monkey
can use it too, but it is a jump!
